model answer_apart
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, M3 C5, gate 8's book/adjust.rs answer_apart (E §5 step 1, L §5.14.3; tally 2.1.8 §4, item 28): a settlement bound over adjustments whose amount is a hole at its day, before the cut, which a later version answers, as any instance's hole booking is; beside it a settlement whose stated amount a later version changes, which is never measured"

source plan "T's invented plan"

source act "T's invented act"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind rents: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

kind fees: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place konto2: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input rent_amt: money PLN

input fee_amt: money PLN

input dom: int

input act_day: date

input back_day: date

input back_amt: money PLN

input fee_back_amt: money PLN

move rent[m in months]: rents
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

move fee[m in months]: fees
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto2 to landlord amount fee_amt

move back[a in adjustments on act_day where a.adjusts in rents]: transfers
  on back_day
  at a.day
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount back_amt
  fulfils a

move fee_back[a in adjustments on act_day where a.adjusts in fees]: transfers
  on back_day
  at a.day
  leg cash from konto2 to landlord amount fee_back_amt
  fulfils a

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 900.00 PLN
  fee_amt = 50.00 PLN
  dom = 10
  act_day = 2026-04-05 governs always
  back_day = 2026-04-20 governs always
  back_amt = ?"how much rent was paid back for March?"
  fee_back_amt = 10.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 5 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version raise
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-05
  replace rent_amt = 1 000.00 PLN
  replace fee_amt = 60.00 PLN

version answer
  cite act
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-05-02
  replace back_amt = 100.00 PLN
  replace fee_back_amt = 25.00 PLN

ask q_bal: bal(konto, d), bal(konto2, d) for d in [2026-04-19, 2026-04-30, 2026-05-31] law cut

ask q_flows: flows(back, 2026-04-01 .. 2026-05-31), flows(fee_back, 2026-04-01 .. 2026-05-31), flows(rent, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-05-31), flows(fee, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-05-31) law cut

ask q_early: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(konto2, 2026-04-30) law cut as known 2026-05-01

ask q_changes: a.change for a in adjustments over .. law cut
